= Learning — Simple =

'''Learning''' is a lasting change caused by experience or practice.

You can learn a fact, a skill, a pattern, a habit, or a better way to solve a problem.

Learning is not the same as doing well once. A lucky guess or a temporary boost is not enough; learning should change what you can do or know later.

Learning is closely connected to [[Memory/Simple|memory]], because learned information has to affect later thinking or behavior.

People learn in many ways, including practice, feedback, observation, association, and discovering patterns.

Human learning is different from [[Machine learning|machine learning]], even though both involve change from experience or data.

